            <ArticleTitle>[Combination and sequential therapy using bisphosphonates.]</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>263-271</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">CliCa1702263271</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Bisphosphonates have been explored possible combination and/or sequential use with other anti-osteoporotic medications including PTH. Besides with vitamin D(metabolites), combination treatment had been uncommon mainly because there had not been enough anti-fracture evidence. PTH, which can only be used for a certain period over lifetime, requires other anti-osteoporotic medications after and/or before its use. Bisphosphonates have been tried with PTH in various sequential and/or combination ways. Various combination and/or sequential therapy using bisphosphonates will be reviewed in this article.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
